remstart
    THE BIG MOMENTS
    the first few times that something big happens in a game, the game slows down for it, so that a new
    player can see what happened. the pops hold back for a moment, the corners of the screen get darker,
    the screen knocks, and the name of what happened pops up where it happened: "Belly Up!", "Schooling
    Fish!", "Coral Song Done!", "Rainbow Fish!" and "Wild Rainbow!". then the words burst into bubbles.

    it eases off. the first time in a game is the whole show (TEACH_FULL). the second time the hold is
    shorter, and the corners only get a little darker (TEACH_SHORT). the third time it is only the words,
    and nothing waits for them (TEACH_WORDS). after that, nothing.

    a player who has seen a moment TEACH_LIFE_CAP times, over all of their games, knows it: from then on
    it only gets the words, the first time in a game, and never holds anything up. the counts are kept
    in the preferences, from TEACH_PREF. FISH_TEACH_RESET=1 forgets them every time the game starts.

    "Pop Speed" on the options page is "Regular", which is all of the above, or "Fast", which is none
    of it. the demo always plays it as a new player would see it, whatever the option says, and it
    keeps nothing (see THE DEMO in fish_headers_demo). the little boards of the first dive have their
    own words, so there is none of this while they are up. and the tests turn it off.

    ONE MOMENT, FROM START TO FINISH. everything from the first words until the board settles is one
    moment. the corners get dark when the first words come up, and stay dark through every pop and fall
    of the run, however many looks it takes; they only get light again once the board has settled and
    the last words have burst. a moment that happens more than once in the run is only counted once: its
    words give a little jump, if they are still up, and nothing more is held for it.

    MORE THAN ONE AT ONCE. a pop can teach several things: a new rainbow fish, a school, and a belly up
    fish, all in one look. each gets its turn, one after the other: its words pop up where it happened, the
    pops wait for it, and then its words burst into bubbles, in their color, out of the way of the next
    one. the second and later of one look hold a little less (TEACH_HOLD_MORE_PERCENT). there are
    TEACH_LINES_MAX of them in a moment at the most.

    HOW IT HOLDS. handle_combos works out every pop of a look before any of them is animated: each one
    is given a delay, and the pops wait for ghostWait. so a moment is claimed (teachClaim) as soon as it
    is known, before the delays of the fish that it is about are worked out, and its hold goes onto
    ghostWait, so the pops after that wait for it, and so do its words: they come up at the ghostWait it
    was claimed at. a moment that is only known for sure once the look has been judged (a coral song) is
    claimed at the start of the look, and shown (teachShow) once it has happened; when it did not
    happen after all, the claim is dropped, and nothing was held up, because a look that pops nothing is
    not animated. teachClaimFree is for a moment that is only known after the delays of the fish before
    it are worked out: it holds nothing, and its words come up when they are told to. the moves that
    the player presses while the pops are held wait in the queue until they go.
    fish_routines_teach has all of it.
remend

#constant TEACH_NONE 0
#constant TEACH_BELLY_UP 1
#constant TEACH_SCHOOL 2
#constant TEACH_CORAL_SONG 3
#constant TEACH_RAINBOW_NEW 4
#constant TEACH_RAINBOW_WILD 5
global TEACH_KINDS = 6 `one more than the last kind, so that the kinds can be used as indexes

` how much of a moment is shown
#constant TEACH_OFF 0
#constant TEACH_FULL 1
#constant TEACH_SHORT 2
#constant TEACH_WORDS 3
` TEACH_AGAIN is a moment that is up already, in this moment. its words jump, and that is all.
#constant TEACH_AGAIN 4

` THE POP SPEED option, on the options page. it is kept between runs of the game. see THE OPTIONS in fish_headers.
#constant PREF_POP_SPEED 19
#constant POP_SPEED_REGULAR 0
#constant POP_SPEED_FAST 1
global OPTION_POP_SPEED = 0

global TEACH_ENABLED = 1 `0 and no moment is ever shown. the tests turn it off.
global TEACH_PREF = 7000 `how many times each moment has been seen, over every game, one number for each kind. it must not move.
global TEACH_LIFE_CAP = 12 `a moment that has been seen this many times, over every game, only gets its words
global dim TEACH_GAME(TEACH_KINDS) `how many times each moment has been shown, this game
global dim TEACH_LIFE(TEACH_KINDS) `and over every game, from the preferences
global dim TEACH_KEY$(TEACH_KINDS) `the words of each, as a key of the strings
global dim TEACH_COLOR(TEACH_KINDS) `the color of its words. 0 for the colors of the rainbow.
global dim TEACH_COLOR_PART#(TEACH_KINDS * 3) `and the same color as red, green and blue, from 0 to 1, for the dark of the spotlight

` how long the pops are held for, how dark the corners get (0 to 1), how hard the screen knocks, and how
` big the words are, for TEACH_FULL and TEACH_SHORT. TEACH_WORDS holds nothing and darkens nothing.
global TEACH_HOLD_FULL_MS = 1100
global TEACH_HOLD_SHORT_MS = 550
global TEACH_HOLD_MORE_PERCENT = 70 `how much of that the second and later moments of one look hold for
global TEACH_DARK_FULL# = 1
global TEACH_DARK_SHORT# = .5
global TEACH_SHAKE_FULL# = 7
global TEACH_SHAKE_SHORT# = 4
global TEACH_SHAKE_MS = 450
global TEACH_TEXT_FULL_H = 34
global TEACH_TEXT_SHORT_H = 28
global TEACH_TEXT_WORDS_H = 24
global TEACH_TEXT_W = 230 `the words are never wider than this, in any language
global TEACH_POP_MS = 220 `how long the words take to pop up
global TEACH_WORDS_MS = 700 `how long words that hold nothing stay up before they burst
global TEACH_READ_MS = 150 `how long after the last words have burst the dark starts to lift, at the least
global TEACH_GONE_MS = 450 `how long the score takes to fade away
global TEACH_PUNCH_MS = 260 `how long the words of a moment that happens again jump for
global TEACH_DARK_IN_MS = 200 `how long the corners take to get dark
global TEACH_DARK_OUT_MS = 500 `and to get light again

` the words of the moments, one line for each
global TEACH_LINES_MAX = 6

` the claims of the look at the board that is going on, one for each kind
global dim TEACH_PEND_LEVEL(TEACH_KINDS) `how much of it will be shown, or TEACH_OFF for no claim
global dim TEACH_PEND_AT(TEACH_KINDS) `when its words come up, in milliseconds after the look
global dim TEACH_PEND_HOLD(TEACH_KINDS) `how long the pops are held for it
global TEACH_LOOK_NEW = 0 `how many new moments this look has claimed
global TEACH_CLAIM_MS = 0 `teachClaim leaves the hold that it adds here. handle_combos adds it to ghostWait.

` the moment that is on the screen
global TEACH_SHOWING = 0 `1 from the first words until the dark has lifted
global TEACH_SETTLED_MS = -1 `when the board settled, or -1 while it has not
global TEACH_HOLD_END_MS = 0 `when the last hold is over. moves wait until then.
global TEACH_READY_MS = 0 `when the last words have burst
global TEACH_FADE_MS = -1 `when the dark starts to lift, or -1 while the moment is still going
global TEACH_DARK# = 0 `how dark the corners get, for the darkest moment so far
global TEACH_VIGNETTE# = 0 `how dark the corners are on this frame. teachStepCorners tells the screen effect.
global TEACH_VIGNETTE_MS = 0 `the frame that it was worked out on
global TEACH_SHAKING = 0 `1 while the knock of a moment is moving the screen
global TEACH_FOUND = -1 `what teachFindLine found
global TEACH_LINE_COUNT = 0
global dim TEACH_LINE_KIND(TEACH_LINES_MAX)
global dim TEACH_LINE_LEVEL(TEACH_LINES_MAX)
global dim TEACH_LINE_AT(TEACH_LINES_MAX) `when its words come up
global dim TEACH_LINE_SLIDE(TEACH_LINES_MAX) `when they burst into bubbles
global dim TEACH_LINE_PUNCH(TEACH_LINES_MAX) `when they last jumped, or -1
global dim TEACH_LINE_X#(TEACH_LINES_MAX) `where it happened
global dim TEACH_LINE_Y#(TEACH_LINES_MAX)
global dim TEACH_LINE_TEXT(TEACH_LINES_MAX)
global dim TEACH_LINE_BUBBLED(TEACH_LINES_MAX) `1 once its words have burst into bubbles
global TEACH_BURST_MS = 220 `how long the words take to burst
global TEACH_BUBBLE_PUFFS = 6 `how many puffs of bubbles they burst into, along them
global dim TEACH_LINE_TIMES(TEACH_LINES_MAX) `how many times it has happened in this moment
global ORDER_TEACH = 34 `over the score texts, and under the info screen

` THE SPOTLIGHT. the dark does not only come in from the corners: it closes in around where the moment
` happened, and the light follows each moment as it comes up, and stays where the last one was until the
` end. the fish that it is about jump while the pops wait for them. and the dark takes
` the color of the moment: blue for a school, pink for coral, green for belly up. see Vignette in ScreenEffect.fx.
global TEACH_SPOT_X# = 0 `where the light is, in pixels of the game, on this frame
global TEACH_SPOT_Y# = 0
global TEACH_TINT_R# = 1 `and the color of the dark, from 0 to 1
global TEACH_TINT_G# = 1
global TEACH_TINT_B# = 1
global TEACH_SPOT_EASE_MS = 140 `how quickly the light and the color follow, in milliseconds. less is quicker.
global TEACH_PULSE_ROOM = 576 `the most cells there can be room for
global dim TEACH_PULSE_NEXT(TEACH_PULSE_ROOM) `when the fish in each cell jumps next
global dim TEACH_PULSE_END(TEACH_PULSE_ROOM) `and when it stops, or 0 for not at all
global TEACH_PULSING = 0 `1 while any fish is
global TEACH_PULSE_GAP = 520 `how far apart the jumps are

global TEACH_COLOR_R# = 1 `what teachColorOf leaves
global TEACH_COLOR_G# = 1
global TEACH_COLOR_B# = 1
global TEACH_PULSE_FROM = 0 `what teachPulseTimes leaves
global TEACH_PULSE_UNTIL = 0

remstart
    NEW IN THE CODEC
    a big moment teaches what happened in a word. the codec says the rest. so when something is found
    that the codec has an entry for, the player is told that there is something new to read in it:
    - the key hint for info mode, at the bottom of the screen, has a little "new info!" that bobs over it.
    - info mode has a "Codec" spot, under the rounds that are left, and while there is something new, a
      "new info!" badge bumps around on it. the confirm key there opens the codec, and it goes straight to
      the first new entry. backing out of it goes straight back to the game.
    - the tiles of the new entries have a dot on them that bobs, until each one has been looked at.
    an entry is new from when it is unlocked (codecSeeCard) until it is highlighted in the codec. what was
    unlocked before any of this was not new, and is not now. a demo unlocks nothing. it is kept in the
    preferences from CODEC_NEW_PREF, one number for each entry.
    the routines are in fish_routines_teach.
remend
global CODEC_NEW_PREF = 7100 `it must not move. there is room for 128 entries.
global dim CODEC_NEW(128) `1 while an entry has been unlocked and not looked at
global CODEC_NEW_COUNT = 0
global CODEC_FIRST_NEW = -1 `what codecNewRecount found: the first new entry, or -1
global CODEC_FROM_INFO = 0 `1 while the codec was opened from info mode, so it goes back to the game
global INFO_INDEX_CODEC = -1 `the spot of info mode
global CODEC_SPOT_X = 0
global CODEC_SPOT_Y = 68
global CODEC_SPOT_W = 108
global CODEC_SPOT_H = 22
global CODEC_SPOT_TEXT_ID = 0 `"Codec", on the spot. it is only there in info mode.
global CODEC_SPOT_BADGE_ID = 0 `"new info!", on the spot
global CODEC_HINT_BADGE_ID = 0 `"new info!", over the key hint
global dim CODEC_NEW_DOTS(32) `the dots on the tiles of the codec
global CODEC_BUMP_GAP = 1600 `how often the badges give a jump, in milliseconds
global CODEC_BUMP_Y# = 0 `what codecBump leaves
global CODEC_BUMP_TURN# = 0

remstart
    THE BADGE ON THE KEY HINT. when something new turns up in the codec, "new info!" pops up beside the
    key hint for info mode, in a small puff of bubbles, and dances there, gently, with a bubble or two
    now and then. it is meant to be noticed, not to nag. after CODEC_DANCE_MS it shrinks, and flies to the corner of the picture of the key,
    where it turns into a little badge, a dot that pulses gently. the badge stays until everything new
    has been read. something new that turns up while the badge is there starts the dance again. a
    game that starts with something new from before only has the badge.
remend
#constant CODEC_BADGE_NONE 0
#constant CODEC_BADGE_DANCE 1
#constant CODEC_BADGE_FLY 2
#constant CODEC_BADGE_DOT 3
global CODEC_BADGE_MODE = 0
global CODEC_BADGE_FROM_MS = 0 `when the dance, or the flight, started
global CODEC_BADGE_KNOWN = -1 `how many new entries there were the last time that codecNewStep looked, or -1 before it has
global CODEC_BADGE_HOP = 0 `which jump of the dance the last puff of bubbles was for
global CODEC_BADGE_DOT_ID = 0 `the dot on the corner of the key
global CODEC_BADGE_FLY_X# = 0 `where the words were when they set off
global CODEC_BADGE_FLY_Y# = 0
global CODEC_DANCE_MS = 5000 `how long "new info!" dances, before it turns into the badge
global CODEC_FLY_MS = 450 `how long it takes to fly to the key
global CODEC_DOT_SIZE = 7 `how big the dot is, in pixels
global CODEC_NEW_LIST_MAX = 6 `info mode lists this many of the new entries by name, and says how many more there are
